// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 21-standard-library-semantics
// facility: rule.stdlib.hashmap `[Lookup-Str]` (D-0113), rule.fn.generic-call (a concrete type argument in a parameter is checked as written); conf.map-get-str-non-string-key-rejected
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.type-mismatch (static)
//
// `contains_str` takes a map keyed by `String`; a `HashMap<u64, i32>`
// is an ordinary type error on the first argument. (The checker once
// accepted this: it bound the parameter's `String` as if it were a type
// parameter. Found 2026-09-30, CHG-0136.)

import std;

fn main()
{
    HashMap<u64, i32> m = HashMap::new();
    HashMap::insert(&mut m, 7, 1);
    bool b = HashMap::contains_str(&m, "k");
}
